    </div>

    <h2>What makes Level 4 tricky<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>The four cards split nineteen moves five, five, five and four, and the split matters less than what the first card asks you to notice. Step 1 sends the girl on the floor to a bed the card calls not fixed. Step 2 is not a drag at all: the timer runs out. Step 3 then calls that bed shaking and puts the hammer by the washing machine into your hand. So the second move needs no gesture, and the third drag waits for it.</p>
    <p>The two girls are the real hazard. Step 1 moves the girl on the floor; step 6 moves the girl lying on the floor. One word apart, different beds, and only step 6 adds that its bed is fixed. Steps 4 and 8 both end at the bed on the left, first with the dancing girl and then with the clean blanket, so that bed takes a person and later takes linen. The washing machine takes two deliveries as well, the dirty quilt at step 7 and the dirty clothes at step 9, while the hammer that starts beside it goes to the shaking bed instead.</p>
    <p>Steps 11 to 14 are four trash piles into one trash can, each named by where it sits: in front of the washing machine, to the right of the table, in the bottom-left corner, and on the table. Four drags, one bin. Step 15 then hands the garbage bag to the flustered girl, her second delivery after the mop at step 10. Step 16 is the only swipe in the level and it opens the bathroom door. What comes out does not go back in: the toilet rag at step 17 goes to the table and the gray cat at step 18 goes to the toilet. Step 19 closes with the perfume and the panicked girl, whom the cards keep separate from the flustered one two cards earlier.</p>

    <h2>Three beds, two girls, one timer<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>Places this level stops a run that is going fine otherwise:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Step 2: the timer runs out. There is nothing to drag, and step 3 cannot land until it does.</li>
      <li>Steps 1 and 6: the girl on the floor and the girl lying on the floor are two people, sent to the bed that is not fixed and the bed that is.</li>
      <li>Steps 4 and 8: the bed on the left takes the dancing girl first, the clean blanket later.</li>
      <li>Steps 7 and 9: the washing machine takes the dirty quilt and the dirty clothes, while the hammer beside it goes to the shaking bed.</li>
      <li>Steps 11 to 14: four trash piles, each named by position, all into one trash can.</li>
      <li>Steps 10 and 15: the flustered girl takes the mop and then the garbage bag.</li>
      <li>Steps 16 to 19: the bathroom door is a swipe; the toilet rag goes to the table, the gray cat to the toilet, the perfume to the panicked girl.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Seventeen drags and one swipe across nineteen moves, and the run only stalls where the timer runs, a label is read wrong or a trash pile is skipped.</p>

    <h2>FAQ<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
   
    <details><summary>What is the answer to Brain Puzzle 3 Level 4?</summary><p>In order: 1) Drag the girl on the floor to the bed (bed not fixed); 2) Time’s up; 3) Drag the hammer by the washing machine to the shaking bed; 4) Drag the dancing girl to the bed on the left; 5) Drag the milky-white paint to the girl who is painting; 6) Drag the girl lying on the floor to the bed on the right (the bed is fixed); 7) Drag the dirty quilt to the washing machine; 8) Drag the clean blanket to the bed on the left; 9) Drag the dirty clothes to the washing machine; 10) Drag the mop to the flustered girl; 11) Drag the trash in front of the washing machine on the floor to the trash can; 12) Drag the trash on the floor to the right of the table to the trash can; 13) Drag the trash on the floor in the bottom-left corner to the trash can; 14) Drag the garbage on the table to the trash can; 15) Drag the garbage bag to the flustered girl; 16) Swipe left to open the bathroom door; 17) Drag the toilet rag to the table; 18) Drag the gray cat to the toilet; 19) Drag the perfume to the panicked girl</p></details>
    <details><summary>Why does nothing happen when I tap in Level 4?</summary><p>Seventeen of the nineteen moves are drags and the only swipe is the bathroom door at step 16, so a tap that does nothing is the wrong gesture for that object.</p></details>
